¶ditem©dbodyy`run_write_loop (libs/autosocket/src/native.rs) retries ws.send(msg.clone()) every 10ms when tungstenite returns Io(WouldBlock). But tungstenite 0.29 stores the frame in its internal write buffer on stream write failure ('will try again on the next call to write or flush'), so send() returning WouldBlock means the frame IS queued and only the flush is incomplete. Each retry therefore enqueues ANOTHER full copy of the frame; as TCP drains, the peer receives thousands of duplicates. Real incident 2026-07-20: levi's facts leg sent a 1457-event batch to levi-hub-01; backpressure kicked in, the retry loop pumped ~3,000 duplicate copies (~4.4M rows in the hub's myko_events table, ~9k events/s) until the client process was killed ‚Äî nearly exhausted the hub's disk. Fix: queue the frame once, then retry ws.flush() only. Also audit wasm.rs for the same pattern.gcreatedx2026-07-21T04:19:07.551283ZlcreatedByDevxtrevor.a.sargent@gmail.compcreatedByMachinegmalcolmbidx a2aefd6b1d394f9b84e546cc0121b833flabelsÅdwirehprioritybP1iprojectIdx de9416570df4447d8687b0103b13ae27etitlexeautosocket: WouldBlock retry duplicates the frame ‚Äî write loop floods the server under backpressurejchangeTypecSEThitemTypedTaskicreatedAtx2026-07-21T04:19:07.551288Zbtxx$e07f43d4-4f3a-4068-aaeb-4c09a38e3d35hsourceIdgmalcolm